es":{"year":"2026 so far: 26 daily record highs, 2 daily record lows","records":"Ely is setting record highs far faster than chance","change":"Ely's nights have warmed since 1986. Its days warmed over the long run.","rain":"Ely has gotten drier"},"text":{"lede":"Yesterday's high of 55\u00b0F was typical for November 13.","t_yest":"November 13: a typical high, but a warm night","p_yest":"The high of <strong>55\u00b0F</strong> was typical for November 13. The normal high for the date is 52\u00b0F, and the record is 70\u00b0F (1999). The low of <strong>31\u00b0F</strong> was the 10th warmest November 13 low (tied) of 104 since 1893.","t_rec":"Ely is setting record highs far faster than chance","p_rec":"If Ely's climate weren't changing, every year would have the same chance of holding a daily record. Since 2000, Ely has set <strong>70 standing record lows</strong>, fewer than the 94 that chance alone would give, and <strong class=\"sig\">186 record highs</strong>, far more than the 94 that chance alone would give. The 2020s hold the most record highs of any decade (82). Ely's all-time high is 101\u00b0F, on July 18, 1998.","t_chg":"Ely's nights have warmed since 1986. Its days warmed over the long run.","p_chg":"Across 96 complete years: Ely's average low shows no clear change: +0.09\u00b0F per decade, a range (\u22120.00 to +0.18) that includes zero. It's close, but the range still includes zero. Ely's average high has risen <strong class='sig'>+0.23\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.14 to +0.32), about +3.0\u00b0F since 1895. <strong>The last 40 years tell a different story:</strong> since 1986, lows have risen <strong class='sig'>+0.51\u00b0F per decade</strong> (95% range +0.12 to +0.91) and highs show no clear change. The full record joins different observing sites over the years, and a move (for example, from the city to a cooler airport) can hide or exaggerate a long-run trend, so the recent decades are the clearer guide here.","t_mon":"Lows rose in 2 of 12 months. Highs rose in 6 of 12 months.","t_rain":"Ely has gotten drier","p_rain":"Ely's yearly precipitation has fallen <strong class='sig'>\u22120.16 inches per decade</strong> (95% range \u22120.32 to \u22120.00), about \u22122.1 inches since 1893. The 1991\u20132020 normal is 9.4 inches a year. The wettest year was 1897 (17.20 in); the driest, 1974 (4.22 in).","show_snow":true,"sig_bars":{"lo":false,"hi":true},"t_year":"2026 so far: 26 daily record highs, 2 daily record lows"}}